Finding 2 — production authority and admission: the free install_bundle facade was removed. First-install and update commands obtain the registered OllamaManager and call manager.install(request). The manager owns admission, operation state, and RecoveryRequired publication on errors. manager_tests::install_error_publishes_recovery_required_and_releases_admission proves the error state and zero active admissions; install_tests::production_install_entrypoint_uses_the_manager_not_a_free_facade guards the command boundary.

Finding 3 — release source authority: latest-version retrieval and fallback_version are owned and re-exported by ollama_manager::release_source. Setup resolution and binary-update checks now delegate there; the old command-local fallback/GitHub helpers were removed. release_source_is_the_only_version_and_fallback_authority and the setup fallback tests cover the boundary.

Finding 4 — redirects: downloads use one bounded redirect policy. It allows the validated GitHub release URL to redirect only to another validated GitHub release URL or an exact HTTPS release-assets.githubusercontent.com/github-production-release-asset/ URL with query, and permits asset-to-asset redirects only. URL length, scheme, exact host, port, credentials, fragment, path, and traversal markers are constrained; hostile HTTP, lookalike hosts, ports, and paths are rejected.

